IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc4-disablement`

-- TESTS for ssc4-disablement.l4 (ss 103-110; ss 102 and 111 are blank in this text). Expected values are written from the text beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- ss 103 to 110`

§§ `s 103 -- disablement pension`

-- s 103(1): the least extent is 14 per cent., or 20 per cent. "on a claim made before 1st October 1986". 30 September 1986 is before; 1 October 1986 is not.
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the least extent of disablement for a claim made on the date, as a percentage` (Date 30 9 1986) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the least extent of disablement for a claim made on the date, as a percentage` (Date 1 10 1986) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the least extent of disablement for a claim made on the date, as a percentage` (Date 1 1 1980) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the least extent of disablement for a claim made on the date, as a percentage` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 14

-- s 103(1): the assessed extent reaches the least extent: 14 on a claim after 1986, 20 before. Not supplied: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` (JUST 14) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` (JUST 13.9) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` (JUST 100) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` (JUST 14) (Date 1 1 1986) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` (JUST 20) (Date 1 1 1986) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` (JUST 19) (Date 30 9 1986) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the assessed extent of the disablement reaches the least extent` NOTHING (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 103(1): an employed earner "shall be entitled to disablement pension if he suffers as the result of the relevant accident from loss of ... faculty such that the assessed extent ... amounts to not less than 14 per cent." Each failed limb of the "if" is FALSE for an employed earner. Not an employed earner, or not known to be: the sentence is silent, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST 14) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST 60) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST 13) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST 60) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST 14) (Date 1 1 1986) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST 60) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST 5) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` NOTHING TRUE (JUST 60) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(1) the person is entitled to disablement pension` NOTHING FALSE (JUST 5) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 103(2): "there may be added ... any present disablement of his (a) which resulted from any other accident ... and (b) in respect of which a disablement gratuity was not paid". Both (a) and (b): may be added. Otherwise the subsection does not say they may not: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the earlier disablement may be added` (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 10 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the earlier disablement may be added` (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 10 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the earlier disablement may be added` (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 10 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the earlier disablement may be added` (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 10 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 103(2): the aggregate is the percentage from the relevant accident plus each permitted earlier disablement, "as well as any percentage which may be so added in accordance with regulations". 30 + 10 + 15 = 55; the item with a gratuity paid (5) and the item from the same accident (20) are not added.
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the aggregate percentage with every addition the subsection permits` 30 (LIST (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 10 TRUE TRUE), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 5 TRUE FALSE), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 20 FALSE TRUE), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 15 TRUE TRUE)) (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 55
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the aggregate percentage with every addition the subsection permits` 30 (LIST (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 10 TRUE TRUE), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 5 TRUE FALSE), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 20 FALSE TRUE), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 15 TRUE TRUE)) (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST 65
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the aggregate percentage with every addition the subsection permits` 30 (LIST (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 10 TRUE TRUE), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 5 TRUE FALSE), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 20 FALSE TRUE), (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 15 TRUE TRUE)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the aggregate percentage with every addition the subsection permits` 30 (LIST (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 5 TRUE FALSE)) (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the aggregate percentage with every addition the subsection permits` 30 (LIST (`s 103(2) Earlier disablement` 10 TRUE TRUE)) (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `s 103(2) the aggregate percentage with every addition the subsection permits` 45 EMPTY (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 45

-- s 103(3): a percentage between 20 and 100 that is not a multiple of 10 is treated, (a) if a multiple of 5, as the next higher multiple of 10; (b) if not, as the nearest multiple of 10. On a claim on or after 1 October 1986, less than 20 but not less than 14 is treated as 20. Otherwise the assessment stands (fork F11).
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 40 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 20 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 100 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 25 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 35 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 45 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 95 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 22 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 24 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 26 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 29 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 21 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 31 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 37 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 96 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 99 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 14 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 15 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 19 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 13 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 5 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 0 (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 15 (Date 30 9 1986) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 19 (Date 1 1 1980) EQUALS 19
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 17 (Date 1 10 1986) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 25 (Date 1 1 1980) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 14 (Date 1 10 1986) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 103(3) the percentage treated as the assessment` 13 (Date 1 10 1986) EQUALS 13

-- s 103(4): where subsection (2) applies, subsection (3) reads the aggregate and not any part of it.
#ASSERT `s 103(4) the percentage to which subsection (3) applies` TRUE 30 55 EQUALS 55
#ASSERT `s 103(4) the percentage to which subsection (3) applies` FALSE 30 55 EQUALS 30

-- s 103(5): "assessed" means assessed in accordance with Schedule 6.
#ASSERT `s 103(5) the extent of the disablement is assessed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(5) the extent of the disablement is assessed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 103(5), second limb: "there shall be taken to be no relevant loss of faculty when the extent ... would not amount to 1 per cent." Below 1: no relevant loss. At 1 or more: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT `s 103(5) there is taken to be no relevant loss of faculty` (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(5) there is taken to be no relevant loss of faculty` (JUST 0.5) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(5) there is taken to be no relevant loss of faculty` (JUST 0.99) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(5) there is taken to be no relevant loss of faculty` (JUST 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(5) there is taken to be no relevant loss of faculty` (JUST 14) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(5) there is taken to be no relevant loss of faculty` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 103(6): "until after the expiry of the period of 90 days (disregarding Sundays) beginning with the day of the relevant accident". Sunday 5 January 2025 is not counted. From Monday 6 January 2025, 90 days not counting Sundays are 15 weeks of 6 days, ending Saturday 19 April 2025. From Saturday 11 January 2025, the 90th such day is Friday 25 April 2025.
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (Date 6 1 2025) 1 EQUALS (Date 6 1 2025)
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (Date 5 1 2025) 1 EQUALS (Date 6 1 2025)
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (Date 11 1 2025) 2 EQUALS (Date 13 1 2025)
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (Date 6 1 2025) 6 EQUALS (Date 11 1 2025)
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (Date 6 1 2025) 7 EQUALS (Date 13 1 2025)
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (Date 6 1 2025) 90 EQUALS (Date 19 4 2025)
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (Date 5 1 2025) 90 EQUALS (Date 19 4 2025)
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the last day of a run of days, not counting Sundays, that begins with the day` (Date 11 1 2025) 90 EQUALS (Date 25 4 2025)
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` (Date 6 1 2025) (Date 6 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` (Date 6 1 2025) (Date 18 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` (Date 6 1 2025) (Date 19 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` (Date 6 1 2025) (Date 20 4 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` (Date 6 1 2025) (Date 21 4 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` (Date 11 1 2025) (Date 19 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` (Date 11 1 2025) (Date 25 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(6) the person is barred from a disablement pension for the day by the 90 days` (Date 11 1 2025) (Date 26 4 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 103(7): where the pension is payable for a period, it is paid at the Schedule 4 rate (a test figure, 150).
#ASSERT `s 103(7) the weekly rate at which the disablement pension is paid in pounds` TRUE (JUST 150) EQUALS JUST 150
#ASSERT `s 103(7) the weekly rate at which the disablement pension is paid in pounds` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(7) the weekly rate at which the disablement pension is paid in pounds` FALSE (JUST 150) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 103(8): where the period is limited by reference to a definite date, the pension ceases on the death of the beneficiary before that date. Death on the date or after it: the sentence is silent.
#ASSERT `s 103(8) the pension ceases on the death of the beneficiary` (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) (JUST (Date 1 5 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(8) the pension ceases on the death of the beneficiary` (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) (JUST (Date 31 5 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 103(8) the pension ceases on the death of the beneficiary` (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(8) the pension ceases on the death of the beneficiary` (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) (JUST (Date 2 6 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(8) the pension ceases on the death of the beneficiary` NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 5 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 103(8) the pension ceases on the death of the beneficiary` (JUST (Date 1 6 2025)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 104 -- increase where constant attendance needed`

-- s 104(1): where a disablement pension is payable in respect of an assessment of 100 per cent., "then, if ... the beneficiary requires constant attendance, the weekly rate of the pension shall be increased". 100 per cent. and attendance: increased. 100 per cent. and no attendance: the "if" fails, FALSE. Other assessment, or no pension: the subsection is not engaged, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the weekly rate of the pension is increased for constant attendance` TRUE 100 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the weekly rate of the pension is increased for constant attendance` TRUE 100 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the weekly rate of the pension is increased for constant attendance` TRUE 99 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the weekly rate of the pension is increased for constant attendance` TRUE 99 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the weekly rate of the pension is increased for constant attendance` FALSE 100 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the weekly rate of the pension is increased for constant attendance` TRUE 90 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 104(1): the increase is an amount determined by regulations, "not exceeding the appropriate amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2" (test figure 50). Fork F12: above the figure, the figure.
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the amount of the increase in pounds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 40) (JUST 50) EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the amount of the increase in pounds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 60) (JUST 50) EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the amount of the increase in pounds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 50) (JUST 50) EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the amount of the increase in pounds` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST 50) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the amount of the increase in pounds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 40) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the amount of the increase in pounds` (JUST FALSE) (JUST 40) (JUST 50) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 104(1) the amount of the increase in pounds` NOTHING (JUST 40) (JUST 50) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 104(4): "“modifications” includes additions and omissions."
#ASSERT `s 104(4) the change is a modification` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104(4) the change is a modification` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 104(2): an increase "shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed from time to time". The period here is 1 July to 31 December 2025, both days inside. A day outside it: the subsection does not say no, since the increase may be renewed, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 104(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 15 9 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 104(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 105 -- increase for exceptionally severe disablement`

-- s 105(1)(a): the weekly rate of the increase "exceeds the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 2(a)" (test figure 50). Equal does not exceed.
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount` (JUST 60) (JUST 50) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount` (JUST 50) (JUST 50) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount` (JUST 40) (JUST 50) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount` NOTHING (JUST 50) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the increase exceeds the amount` (JUST 60) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 105(1): "Where" the pension is payable to a person (a) entitled (or but for in-patient treatment entitled) to a section 104 increase exceeding the paragraph 2(a) amount; and (b) whose need for constant attendance is likely to be permanent, the rate is further increased. A case outside: the section does not address it, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST 60) (JUST 50) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST 50) (JUST 50) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST 60) (JUST 50) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST 60) (JUST 50) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST 60) (JUST 50) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST 50) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the weekly rate of the pension is further increased` TRUE NOTHING (JUST 60) (JUST 50) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 105(1): the further increase is "the amount specified in Schedule 4, Part V, paragraph 3" (test figure 30).
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the amount of the further increase in pounds` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the amount of the further increase in pounds` (JUST FALSE) (JUST 30) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the amount of the further increase in pounds` NOTHING (JUST 30) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105(1) the amount of the further increase in pounds` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 105(2): an increase "shall be payable for such period as may be determined at the time it is granted, but may be renewed from time to time". The period here is 1 July to 31 December 2025, both days inside. A day outside it: the subsection does not say no, since the increase may be renewed, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 105(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 15 9 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 105(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 30 6 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 105(2) the increase is payable on the day` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 7 2025, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 106 -- benefits and increases subject to qualifications as to time`

-- s 106: Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the six named benefits and increases. Another benefit: the section does not say that it has no effect in relation to it, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 106 Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the benefit or increase` `s 106(a) unemployability supplement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 106 Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the benefit or increase` `s 106(b) disablement gratuity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 106 Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the benefit or increase` `s 106(c) an increase of disablement pension during hospital treatment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 106 Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the benefit or increase` `s 106(d) reduced earnings allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 106 Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the benefit or increase` `s 106(e) retirement allowance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 106 Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the benefit or increase` `s 106(f) industrial death benefit` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 106 Schedule 7 has effect in relation to the benefit or increase` `s 106 another benefit or increase` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 107 -- adjustments for successive accidents`

-- s 107(2): the increases referred to in subsection (1) "are those under the following provisions": section 104, section 105, paragraph 2, 4 or 6 of Schedule 7. The list is closed.
#ASSERT `s 107(2) the increase is one referred to in subsection (1)` `s 107(2) section 104` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 107(2) the increase is one referred to in subsection (1)` `s 107(2) section 105` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 107(2) the increase is one referred to in subsection (1)` `s 107(2) paragraph 2 of Schedule 7` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 107(2) the increase is one referred to in subsection (1)` `s 107(2) paragraph 4 of Schedule 7` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 107(2) the increase is one referred to in subsection (1)` `s 107(2) paragraph 6 of Schedule 7` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 107(2) the increase is one referred to in subsection (1)` `s 107(2) another provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 107(1)(a): a person with two or more successive accidents "shall not for the same period be entitled ... to receive ... two or more disablement pensions at an aggregate weekly rate exceeding the appropriate amount" (test figure 100). Above: barred. Equal or below: the bar does not speak, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate rate exceeds the appropriate amount` 120 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate rate exceeds the appropriate amount` 100.01 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate rate exceeds the appropriate amount` 100 (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate rate exceeds the appropriate amount` 80 (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate rate exceeds the appropriate amount` 120 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the person is barred from an aggregate weekly rate above the appropriate amount` TRUE 120 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the person is barred from an aggregate weekly rate above the appropriate amount` TRUE 100 (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the person is barred from an aggregate weekly rate above the appropriate amount` TRUE 80 (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the person is barred from an aggregate weekly rate above the appropriate amount` FALSE 120 (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the person is barred from an aggregate weekly rate above the appropriate amount` TRUE 120 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate weekly rate the person may receive for the same period, apart from increases, in pounds` TRUE 120 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate weekly rate the person may receive for the same period, apart from increases, in pounds` TRUE 80 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 80
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate weekly rate the person may receive for the same period, apart from increases, in pounds` TRUE 100 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate weekly rate the person may receive for the same period, apart from increases, in pounds` FALSE 120 (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 107(1)(a) the aggregate weekly rate the person may receive for the same period, apart from increases, in pounds` TRUE 120 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 108 -- benefit in respect of prescribed industrial diseases, etc.`

-- s 108(1): benefits "shall ... be payable" for a person who has been in employed earner's employment in respect of (a) any prescribed disease, or (b) any prescribed personal injury (other than an injury caused by accident ...), "which is a disease or injury due to the nature of that employment". All met: payable. Otherwise "shall be payable" is not "only if": NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 108(1) industrial injuries benefits are payable in respect of the prescribed disease or injury` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 108(6): a person "shall not be entitled to benefit in respect of a disease as being an injury by accident ... if at the time of the accident the disease is in relation to him a prescribed disease by virtue of the occupation". Prescribed by occupation: barred. Not: the "if" fails, no bar. Unknown: NOTHING. Not such a claim: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 108(6) the person is barred from benefit in respect of a disease as an injury by accident` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 108(6) the person is barred from benefit in respect of a disease as an injury by accident` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 108(6) the person is barred from benefit in respect of a disease as an injury by accident` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 108(6) the person is barred from benefit in respect of a disease as an injury by accident` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 108(6) the person is barred from benefit in respect of a disease as an injury by accident` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 109 -- general provisions relating to benefit under section 108`

-- s 109(1): "Subject to the power to make different provision by regulations, and to the following provisions of this section and section 110", the benefit and conditions "shall be the same as" for personal injury by accident. An exception that applies: not the same. None: the same. Unknown: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(1) the benefit and the conditions for receipt are the same as for personal injury by accident` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 109(2): the Administration Act provisions relating to administration "shall be taken to include section 1 of that Act and any provision which relates to the administration of both the benefit in question and other benefits".
#ASSERT `s 109(2) the provision is taken to relate to the administration of disablement benefit or reduced earnings allowance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 109(2) the provision is taken to relate to the administration of disablement benefit or reduced earnings allowance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 109(2) the provision is taken to relate to the administration of disablement benefit or reduced earnings allowance` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 109(5): "the appropriate percentage" means the assessed percentage of any present disablement which resulted (a) from an accident ... or (b) from any other prescribed disease or injury, and for which a gratuity was not paid.
#ASSERT `s 109(5) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 20 TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 109(5) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 20 FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 109(5) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 20 TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 109(5) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 20 FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(5) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(5) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 20 FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(5) the appropriate percentage for subsection (4)(a)` (LIST (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 20 TRUE FALSE TRUE), (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 30 FALSE TRUE TRUE), (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 15 FALSE FALSE TRUE), (`s 109(5) Present disablement` 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 109(5) the appropriate percentage for subsection (4)(a)` EMPTY EQUALS 0

-- s 109(6): "the appropriate percentage" means the assessed percentage of any present disablement (a) which resulted from any prescribed disease or injury due to the nature of his employment, and (b) for which a gratuity was not paid.
#ASSERT `s 109(6) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(6) Present disablement` 10 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 109(6) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(6) Present disablement` 10 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(6) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(6) Present disablement` 10 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(6) the present disablement counts in the appropriate percentage` (`s 109(6) Present disablement` 10 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 109(6) the appropriate percentage for subsection (4)(b)` (LIST (`s 109(6) Present disablement` 10 TRUE TRUE), (`s 109(6) Present disablement` 5 TRUE FALSE), (`s 109(6) Present disablement` 7 FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 109(6) the appropriate percentage for subsection (4)(b)` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§§ `s 110 -- respiratory diseases`

-- s 110(3): "A person found to be suffering from pneumoconiosis shall be treated ... as suffering from a loss of faculty such that the assessed extent of the resulting disablement amounts to not less than 1 per cent."
#ASSERT `s 110(3) the least assessed extent of the disablement treated as resulting, as a percentage` TRUE EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 110(3) the least assessed extent of the disablement treated as resulting, as a percentage` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 110(4): in respect of byssinosis a person "shall not (unless regulations otherwise provide) be entitled to disablement benefit unless he is found to be suffering ... from loss of faculty which is likely to be permanent". Permanent loss found: no bar. Regulations otherwise provide: no bar. Neither: barred. Regulations unknown and no permanent loss: NOTHING. Not byssinosis: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 110(4) the person is barred from disablement benefit in respect of byssinosis` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
